# .codex/state.db — SQLite State Bus Schema

The `.codex/state.db` file is the shared state bus between Claude and Codex agents. Claude initializes it, agents read/write their own state, and all coordination happens through SQL queries.

## WAL Mode

The database uses WAL (Write-Ahead Logging) mode, which allows:
- **Unlimited concurrent readers** — Claude can read state while agents write
- **Single writer** — Only one process writes at a time (SQLite handles locking)
- **busy_timeout=5000** — Waits up to 5 seconds if the database is locked

## Full Schema

```sql
PRAGMA journal_mode=WAL;
PRAGMA busy_timeout=5000;

-- Mission state (singleton row)
CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS mission (
  id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY CHECK (id = 1),
  stage TEXT NOT NULL,
  mission TEXT NOT NULL,
  started_at TEXT NOT NULL,
  updated_at TEXT NOT NULL,
  progress TEXT DEFAULT '',
  blockers TEXT DEFAULT '[]',
  next_steps TEXT DEFAULT '[]',
  summary TEXT DEFAULT ''
);

-- Agents registry
CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS agents (
  id TEXT PRIMARY KEY,
  task TEXT NOT NULL,
  status TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'pending'
    CHECK (status IN ('pending', 'running', 'completed', 'failed')),
  sandbox TEXT DEFAULT 'workspace-write',
  started_at TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT (strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', 'now')),
  completed_at TEXT,
  files_modified TEXT DEFAULT '[]',
  summary TEXT DEFAULT ''
);

-- Event history
CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS events (
  id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT,
  timestamp TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT (strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', 'now')),
  type TEXT NOT NULL CHECK (type IN (
    'course_correction', 'approval', 'abort', 'info',
    'stage_change', 'agent_spawn', 'agent_start', 'agent_complete', 'agent_fail'
  )),
  source TEXT NOT NULL,
  message TEXT NOT NULL,
  context TEXT
);

-- File locks (prevents concurrent modification)
CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS file_locks (
  file_path TEXT PRIMARY KEY,
  agent_id TEXT NOT NULL,
  locked_at TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT (strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', 'now')),
  FOREIGN KEY (agent_id) REFERENCES agents(id)
);

-- Agent progress checkpoints
CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS checkpoints (
  id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT,
  agent_id TEXT NOT NULL,
  timestamp TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT (strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', 'now')),
  message TEXT NOT NULL,
  FOREIGN KEY (agent_id) REFERENCES agents(id)
);

-- Indexes for common queries
CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_events_source ON events(source);
CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_events_type ON events(type);
CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_checkpoints_agent ON checkpoints(agent_id);
```

## Table Descriptions

### `mission` — Singleton orchestration state
| Column | Type | Description |
|--------|------|-------------|
| id | INTEGER | Always 1 (singleton row) |
| stage | TEXT | Current pipeline stage |
| mission | TEXT | Human-readable mission description |
| started_at | TEXT | ISO 8601 timestamp when mission started |
| updated_at | TEXT | ISO 8601 timestamp of last state update |
| progress | TEXT | Human-readable progress summary |
| blockers | TEXT | JSON array of current blockers |
| next_steps | TEXT | JSON array of next steps |
| summary | TEXT | Final mission summary |

### `agents` — Agent registry
| Column | Type | Description |
|--------|------|-------------|
| id | TEXT | codex-agent job ID (primary key) |
| task | TEXT | Description of assigned task |
| status | TEXT | pending, running, completed, or failed |
| sandbox | TEXT | read-only or workspace-write |
| started_at | TEXT | ISO 8601 timestamp (auto-set) |
| completed_at | TEXT | ISO 8601 timestamp when finished (null if running) |
| files_modified | TEXT | JSON array of modified file paths |
| summary | TEXT | Agent's completion summary |

### `events` — Event history
| Column | Type | Description |
|--------|------|-------------|
| id | INTEGER | Auto-increment primary key |
| timestamp | TEXT | ISO 8601 timestamp (auto-set) |
| type | TEXT | Event type (see below) |
| source | TEXT | Who created the event (claude, agent-{id}) |
| message | TEXT | Event message |
| context | TEXT | Additional context (optional) |

**Event types:** stage_change, agent_spawn, agent_start, agent_complete, agent_fail, course_correction, approval, abort, info

### `file_locks` — Concurrent file modification prevention
| Column | Type | Description |
|--------|------|-------------|
| file_path | TEXT | Absolute or relative file path (primary key) |
| agent_id | TEXT | Foreign key to agents.id |
| locked_at | TEXT | ISO 8601 timestamp (auto-set) |

### `checkpoints` — Agent progress reports
| Column | Type | Description |
|--------|------|-------------|
| id | INTEGER | Auto-increment primary key |
| agent_id | TEXT | Foreign key to agents.id |
| timestamp | TEXT | ISO 8601 timestamp (auto-set) |
| message | TEXT | Progress update message |

## Write Ownership

| Table | Writer | Reader |
|-------|--------|--------|
| `mission` | Claude only | Claude, Codex agents |
| `agents` (INSERT) | Claude only | Claude, Codex agents |
| `agents` (UPDATE own row) | Each agent by ID | Claude, Codex agents |
| `events` | Claude (source='claude'), Agents (source='agent-{id}') | Claude, Codex agents |
| `file_locks` | Codex agents (claim on start, release on finish) | Claude, Codex agents |
| `checkpoints` | Codex agents (progress updates during work) | Claude, Codex agents |

## Common Query Patterns

### Read mission state
```bash
sqlite3 -header -column .codex/state.db "SELECT stage, mission, progress, blockers, next_steps FROM mission WHERE id=1;"
```

### Read all agent statuses
```bash
sqlite3 -header -column .codex/state.db "SELECT id, task, status, files_modified, summary FROM agents;"
```

### Read running agents only
```bash
sqlite3 -header -column .codex/state.db "SELECT id, task, started_at FROM agents WHERE status IN ('pending','running');"
```

### Read recent checkpoints
```bash
sqlite3 -header -column .codex/state.db "SELECT agent_id, timestamp, message FROM checkpoints ORDER BY id DESC LIMIT 20;"
```

### Read Claude decisions
```bash
sqlite3 -header -column .codex/state.db "SELECT timestamp, type, message FROM events WHERE source='claude' ORDER BY id;"
```

### Check file locks
```bash
sqlite3 -header -column .codex/state.db "SELECT file_path, agent_id FROM file_locks;"
```

### Register a new agent
```bash
sqlite3 .codex/state.db "INSERT INTO agents (id, task, sandbox) VALUES ('{id}', '{task}', '{sandbox}');"
```

### Claim a file lock
```bash
sqlite3 .codex/state.db "INSERT OR IGNORE INTO file_locks (file_path, agent_id) VALUES ('{path}', '{id}');"
```

### Write a checkpoint
```bash
sqlite3 .codex/state.db "INSERT INTO checkpoints (agent_id, message) VALUES ('{id}', '{progress message}');"
```

### Mark agent complete
```bash
sqlite3 .codex/state.db "UPDATE agents SET status='completed', completed_at=strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ','now'), files_modified='{json_array}', summary='{summary}' WHERE id='{id}';"
sqlite3 .codex/state.db "DELETE FROM file_locks WHERE agent_id='{id}';"
```

### Update mission progress
```bash
sqlite3 .codex/state.db "UPDATE mission SET progress='{progress}', updated_at=strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ','now') WHERE id=1;"
```

## What Stays as Files

| File | Reason |
|------|--------|
| `.codex/reviews/codex-*.md` | Freeform markdown documents, agents write directly |
| `.codex/reviews/synthesis.md` | Freeform markdown document, Claude writes |
